{"candidate_id":"c_1bc4aee7770545f2","chunk_id":"eor_-130814_06e54c49#c000","evidence":{"char_end":1267,"char_start":0,"chunk_id":"eor_-130814_06e54c49#c000","doc_id":"eor_-130814_06e54c49","grounding":"none","span":"eor_-130814_06e54c49:0-1267","text":"Temporarily abandon VK 826 A013. The Chris K was squeezed and abandoned with coil tubing prior to temporary abandonment operations.\nTubing was cut at 10,165' MD and pulled from the well. \nRelease mudline packer and pull downhole equipment. Note, could not get down and found large amounts of paraffin when tool string was recovered. Went to secondary release mechanism for mudline packer.\nSet bridge plug and set 200' cement plug on top of CIBP, then used a retrievable packer to isolate leak. See attached verbal approval for reference.\nPOH with retrievable packer and set cement retainer at 5,600' MD, pump 19 bbls of cement and squeeze casing leak at 5,623' MD-5,639' MD. Pressure test casing to 1500 psi for 15 minutes.\nSpot 50' cement plug on top of retainer to leave TOC at 5,550' MD. Pressure test casing to 1500 psi for 15 minutes.\nSet cement retainer w/ TCP at 4,384' MD, perforate 9 5/8\" casing from 4,500'-4,504'. 9 5/8\" x 13 3/8\" annulus postive and negative tested. 50' cement on top of cement retainer, TOC at 4,334' MD. Test casing and plug to 1500 psi.\nSet cement retainer w/ TCP at 2,835' MD, 9 5/8\" and 13 5/8\" casing perforated from 2,950'-2,954' MD. 13 3/8\" x 20\" annulus postive and negative tested. Cement plug on top of retainer, TOC 2,285' MD."},"extractor":"guided","extractor_version":"kgb/0.1.0;extract=guided@bsee_guided:304bf4be;llm=qwen3.6-35b-a3b","object":"Temporarily abandon","predicate":"has_well_status","source_doc_id":"eor_-130814_06e54c49","subject":"well","temporal_marker":null,"time_iso":null,"trigger_relation":null}
